Corrected code: 

pipeline {
    agent any

    environment {
        APP_ENV = 'staging'
    }

    stages {

        stage('Build') {
            steps {
                retry(3) {
                    sh 'make build'
                }
            }
        }

        stage('Test') {
            steps {
                script {
                    try {
                        sh 'make test'
                    } catch (err) {
                        currentBuild.result = 'UNSTABLE'
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}

Changes made to convert scripted piprline into declarative pipeline


node { ... } is Scripted Pipeline syntax.
Change: Use pipeline { agent any ... } in Declarative Pipeline.

env.APP_ENV = 'staging' is Scripted-style environment assignment.
Change: Use environment { APP_ENV = 'staging' }.

stage('Build') is inside the node block.
Change: Put stages inside the required stages { ... } block.

retry(3) is directly inside the Scripted stage.
Change: Put retry(3) inside the Declarative steps { ... } block.

try/catch is Groovy logic.
Change: Use script { ... } because Declarative does not allow arbitrary Groovy directly inside steps.

